# VitalWatch — Health Monitoring Dashboard

A real-time health monitoring web app with live ECG simulation, vital sign tracking, and an alert engine. Built with vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript — no frameworks, no dependencies.

![screenshot](screenshot.png)

## Features

- Live vitals: Heart rate, SpO₂, Blood pressure, Temperature
- Animated ECG trace (Lead II simulation)
- Sparkline trend charts per vital
- Auto alert log with severity levels (ok / warn / danger)
- Risk badge that updates in real time
- Pause/resume monitoring
- Fully responsive (mobile + desktop)

## Project structure

```
health-monitor/
├── index.html   # App shell and layout
├── style.css    # Dark clinical theme
├── app.js       # Vitals engine, ECG, charts, alerts
└── README.md
```

## Run locally

Just open `index.html` in any browser — no build step needed.

```bash
# Or serve with Python
python3 -m http.server 8080
# Then open http://localhost:8080
```

## Deploy to GitHub Pages

1. Create a new repo on GitHub (e.g. `health-monitor`)
2. Push this project:

```bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit: VitalWatch health monitor"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/health-monitor.git
git push -u origin main
```

3. Go to **Settings → Pages → Source → Deploy from branch → main / root**
4. Your live URL will be: `https://YOUR_USERNAME.github.io/health-monitor/`

## Extend it

| Feature | How |
|---|---|
| Real device data | Replace `generateVitals()` in `app.js` with a WebSocket or BLE API call |
| Patient records | Add a `patients.json` and a sidebar to switch patients |
| Backend alerts | POST to a Node/FastAPI endpoint from `addAlert()` |
| Historical charts | Swap sparklines for Chart.js with date-range controls |
| Auth | Add a login screen before `<main>` renders |

## Tech stack

- HTML5 Canvas (ECG + sparklines)
- CSS custom properties + Grid + Flexbox
- Vanilla JS (no dependencies)
- Google Fonts: Syne + DM Mono

